      ":question/problem": "Rewrite the following expression as the sum of a perfect square and a constant.\n\n$({y}^{2}+10y+25)+8=(${{field-1}}${)}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we recall the following formula:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+2ay+{a}^{2}=(y+a{)}^{2}\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a perfect square in the parentheses that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+10y+25 & = \\\\ {y}^{2}+2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2} & = \\\\ (y+5{)}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}^{2}+10y+25)+8 & = \\\\ (y+5{)}^{2}+8 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
